        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Identify Intent and Extract Shipment"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777391996806"
          },
          "code": "IDENTIFY_INTENT",
          "id": "1773427701443",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773427701444_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Task1 - Classify the user’s message into exactly ONE intent label:\nCHANGE_SERVICE_PROVIDER | SECURE_RESOURCE | ACCEPT_TENDER | DECLINE_TENDER | NOT_SUPPORTED\n\nRules:\n- Output only one label. Do not explain.\n\n1. CHANGE_SERVICE_PROVIDER\nUse only when the user explicitly wants to change, switch, replace, or update the carrier, service provider, or logistics provider.\nDo NOT use this label for changing equipment, equipment group, location, shipment details, dates, reference numbers, or other attributes.\nExamples:\n- \"change carrier\" -> CHANGE_SERVICE_PROVIDER\n- \"switch service provider\" -> CHANGE_SERVICE_PROVIDER\n- \"change equipment group\" -> NOT_SUPPORTED\n\n2. SECURE_RESOURCE\nUse only when the user explicitly wants to secure resources, or tender shipments.\nDo NOT use this label for accepting, declining, changing providers, or other unrelated updates.\nExamples:\n- \"secure resource\" -> SECURE_RESOURCE\n- \"tender shipment\" -> SECURE_RESOURCE\n\n3. ACCEPT_TENDER\nUse only when the user explicitly wants to accept, approve, confirm a tender.\nDo NOT use this label for changing providers, securing resources, or declining tenders.\nExamples:\n- \"accept the tender\" -> ACCEPT_TENDER\n- \"confirm for shipment\" -> ACCEPT_TENDER\n- \"modify tender\" -> NOT_SUPPORTED\n\n4. DECLINE_TENDER\nUse only when the user explicitly wants to decline, reject, or refuse tender.\nDo NOT use this label for changing providers, securing resources, or accepting tenders.\nExamples:\n- \"decline the tender\" -> DECLINE_TENDER\n- \"reject this shipment\" -> DECLINE_TENDER\n- \"withdraw tender\" -> NOT_SUPPORTED\n\n5. NOT_SUPPORTED\nUse when the request is outside these four actions, ambiguous, or refers to unsupported changes such as equipment group changes, route changes, rate changes, or other unsupported maintenance.\nWhen in doubt, choose NOT_SUPPORTED.\nExamples:\n- \"change cost\" -> NOT_SUPPORTED\n- \"update origin location\" -> NOT_SUPPORTED\n- \"change rate offering\" -> NOT_SUPPORTED\n\n\nTask2 - Extract shipment identifiers from the user message:\nExtraction rules (in priority order):\n1. Explicit shipment mention (highest confidence):\n- If the message contains labels like shipment, shipment gid, shipment xid, ship gid, ship id, sh gid, sh id, extract the identifier(s) immediately following (or clearly associated with) that label.\n- Support multiple identifiers if present (comma/space/newline/“and” separated).\n2. Implied shipment context (medium confidence):\n- If the message contains phrases such as for <id>, on <id> in the context of shipment actions (e.g., \"change service provider\", \"secure resource\", \"accept tender\"), treat the referenced <id> value(s) as shipment identifier(s) even if the word “shipment” is not present.\n- Support multiple identifiers in this implied form, including patterns like: “for <id1> and <id2>”, “for <id1>, <id2>, <id3>”, “on <id1> <id2>”\n\nNormalization:\n- Uppercase every extracted shipment identifier and put in an string array.\n- If not found, return empty array.\n\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this exact schema:\n{\n  \"intent\":\"<LABEL>\",\n  \"shipment\": [\"<SHIPMENT_1>\", \"<SHIPMENT_2>\"]\n}\n\nMessage:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"shipment\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
