              "id": "1774361536885_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Task 1 - You are given {{$context.$variables.invalidShipmentArr}}. Summarize these invalid shipments in this exact text: \"Invalid shipments to decline tender: \".\nIf no value is present, DO NOT output any text.\n\nTask 2 - You are given a JSON object. Output \"Tender declined for the following shipments:\" first. Then summarize the JSON object in a HTML table with column headers on the first row and values on the second row. Only use the array under the key \"items\".\n\nUser Current DateTime: {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\nColumns (in this exact order) and mapping:\n1. Shipment: shipmentPk\n2. Total Actual Cost: totalActualCost.value + totalActualCost.currency with value rounded to 2 decimals (example: 99.99 USD).\n3. Total Weighted Cost: totalWeightedCost.value + totalWeightedCost.currency with value rounded to 2 decimals.\n4. Start Time: convert startTime.value from ISO 8601 into format \"YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss\", adjusting from UTC (\"Z\") to match the timezone of the User Current DateTime.\n5. End Time: convert endTime.value using the same format and timezone rules as Start Time.\n6. Service Provider: serviceProviderID\n7. Rate Offering: rateOffering\n\nIf JSON object 1 is null, use JSON object 2.\nJSON object 1:\n{{$context.$nodes.DECLINE_TENDERS.$output}}\nJSON object 2:\n{{$context.$nodes.DECLINE_SINGLE_TENDER.$output}} \n\nOutput only:\n1. The invalid shipments text (conditionally)\n2. The HTML table"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
