              "id": "1775151780371_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given a JSON object as input.\n\nExtract:\n- count\n- all shipment records containing:\n  - domainName\n  - shipmentXid\n\nFor each shipment record, generate shipmentGid using these rules:\n- If domainName is exactly \"PUBLIC\", shipmentGid = shipmentXid\n- Otherwise, shipmentGid = domainName + \".\" + shipmentXid\n\nCollect all generated shipmentGid values into the shipment array.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this exact format:\n{\n  \"count\": <count>,\n  \"shipment\": [\n    \"<shipmentGid1>\",\n    \"<shipmentGid2>\"\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n- shipment must always be a string array\n- Preserve the original order of shipment records\n- Do not include duplicate fields or extra text\n- Return valid JSON only\n\nJSON object input:\n{{$context.$nodes.CHECK_SHIPMENT_FOR_ACCEPT_TENDER.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"shipment\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"count\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
